          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Iterable vs Iterator",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Iterable",
                "Iterator"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Has",
                  "`__iter__()`",
                  "`__next__()` and `__iter__()`"
                ],
                [
                  "`__iter__()` returns",
                  "a new iterator",
                  "{green:self}"
                ],
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "list, tuple, dict, str",
                  "file object, `iter([1,2])` (list_iterator)"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What a for loop does",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "iter(obj)",
                    "sub": "called once",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next()",
                    "sub": "repeated",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "StopIteration",
                    "sub": "loop ends",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Exhaustion and defaults",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "An iterator is ==single-pass== and **stateful**",
                "When exhausted, `next()` keeps raising `StopIteration`",
                "`next(it, default)` returns ==default== instead of raising"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "it = iter([1, 2])",
                "print(type(it).__name__)",
                "print(next(it), next(it))",
                "print(next(it, \"done\"))",
                "print(next(it, \"done\"))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "list_iterator",
                "1 2",
                "done",
                "done"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Reusable vs one-shot",
              "text": "A list can be looped again; its iterator cannot. A `for` over an exhausted iterator runs ==zero times== with no error."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Generators and yield",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Generators and yield",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Generator basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A function with `yield` returns a ==generator object== when called",
                "The body does **not run** until the first `next()`",
                "`yield` ==pauses== and keeps locals; the next `next()` resumes right after it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Finishing and delegating",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Falling off the end or a bare `return` raises ==StopIteration==",
                "The `return` value becomes `StopIteration.value`",
                "`yield from sub` delegates to a sub-iterable, ==passes its return value back=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def gen():",
                "    yield 1",
                "    return \"done\"",
                "g = gen()",
                "print(next(g))",
                "try:",
                "    next(g)",
                "except StopIteration as e: print(e.value)"
              ],
              "note": "return value rides on StopIteration"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1",
                "done"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. send and close",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`next(g)`",
                  "resumes; `yield` evaluates to None"
                ],
                [
                  "`g.send(x)`",
                  "paused `yield` evaluates to x"
                ],
                [
                  "`g.close()`",
                  "raises `GeneratorExit` inside"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Prime first",
              "text": "Call `next(g)` once before `send(x)`; a non-None send to a fresh generator raises TypeError."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Does calling it run it?** No, the first `next()` does",
                "**Where does return go?** `StopIteration.value`",
                "**What does close() do?** Raises `GeneratorExit` inside"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
