    {
      "title": "Context Managers and with",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Context Managers and with",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The with Protocol",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`with obj as x:` calls ==`__enter__()`== and binds its return value to `x`",
                "Always calls ==`__exit__(exc_type, exc, tb)`== on the way out",
                "{green:Truthy} return from `__exit__` **suppresses** the exception",
                "`None` or {red:False} lets it propagate"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. @contextmanager",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@contextlib.contextmanager` turns a generator with ==one yield== into a manager",
                "Wrap `yield` in ==try/finally== so cleanup runs on errors"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from contextlib import contextmanager",
                "@contextmanager",
                "def cm():",
                "    res = setup()",
                "    try:",
                "        yield res",
                "    finally:",
                "        cleanup()"
              ],
              "note": "the yielded value becomes the as target"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No try/finally",
              "text": "The body's exception is raised at `yield`, so cleanup code after it is **skipped**."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Everyday Helpers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Helper",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`suppress(Err)`",
                  "ignores that exception"
                ],
                [
                  "`closing(obj)`",
                  "calls `obj.close()` on exit"
                ],
                [
                  "`ExitStack`",
                  "dynamic number of managers"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`with a, b:` enters ==left to right==, exits in **reverse**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
